# Skill source tracking — mattpocock/skills vendored skills

This file is the shared update-check manifest for every local skill vendored from
https://github.com/mattpocock/skills. The check runs when the grilling skill is
invoked (directly, or through /devflow), at most once per 7-day window.

upstream_repo: https://github.com/mattpocock/skills
upstream_releases_url: https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/releases
upstream_latest_release_url: https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/releases/latest
upstream_changelog_url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mattpocock/skills/main/CHANGELOG.md

check_window_days: 7
last_checked: never

# Every vendored file tracked by this manifest. local body = the local SKILL.md with
# any local-enhancement block (between the two comment markers) stripped.
tracked_files:
  grilling:
    upstream_path: skills/productivity/grilling/SKILL.md
    upstream_raw_url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mattpocock/skills/main/skills/productivity/grilling/SKILL.md
    local_path: skills/grilling/SKILL.md
    last_known_commit_sha: 86cba45f4244b2545112d13e77ba82eb2bfad325
    last_known_commit_date: 2026-08-15
    last_known_commit_message: Remove em-dashes from grilling skill
  domain-modeling:
    upstream_path: skills/engineering/domain-modeling/SKILL.md
    upstream_raw_url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mattpocock/skills/main/skills/engineering/domain-modeling/SKILL.md
    local_path: skills/devflow/domain-modeling/SKILL.md
    last_known_commit_sha: unknown
    last_known_commit_date: unknown
    last_known_commit_message: unknown
  tdd:
    upstream_path: skills/engineering/tdd/SKILL.md
    upstream_raw_url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mattpocock/skills/main/skills/engineering/tdd/SKILL.md
    local_path: skills/devflow/tdd/SKILL.md
    last_known_commit_sha: unknown
    last_known_commit_date: unknown
    last_known_commit_message: unknown
  to-spec:
    upstream_path: skills/engineering/to-spec/SKILL.md
    upstream_raw_url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mattpocock/skills/main/skills/engineering/to-spec/SKILL.md
    local_path: skills/devflow/to-spec/SKILL.md
    last_known_commit_sha: unknown
    last_known_commit_date: unknown
    last_known_commit_message: unknown
  to-tickets:
    upstream_path: skills/engineering/to-tickets/SKILL.md
    upstream_raw_url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mattpocock/skills/main/skills/engineering/to-tickets/SKILL.md
    local_path: skills/devflow/to-tickets/SKILL.md
    last_known_commit_sha: unknown
    last_known_commit_date: unknown
    last_known_commit_message: unknown

# Check rule (for the agent reading this file):
# If last_checked is "never" or (today - last_checked) >= 7 days, perform the check over
# EVERY file in tracked_files. Otherwise skip the check entirely and proceed.
#   1. For each tracked file: fetch its upstream_raw_url, read its local_path, strip the
#      local-enhancement block (between the two comment markers) from the local file, and
#      compare the remote content with the local upstream body, character for character.
#   2. Update last_checked to today's date (YYYY-MM-DD) after the pass, regardless of results.
#   3. For every file whose contents differ: do NOT just dump the diff. Fetch the official
#      release notes / CHANGELOG (upstream_latest_release_url and/or upstream_changelog_url),
#      find the changes that touch that skill, cross-check them against the actual content
#      diff, and give the user a recommendation per skill: what the change means, whether
#      it's worth updating, and any risks. Watch out for local customisations: if the local
#      file was deliberately customised, say so and let the user decide. NEVER modify any
#      SKILL.md without explicit user confirmation.
#   4. If the check fails (network/API), skip it silently and proceed — never block the interview.
